{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Eightfold.ConnectedSumAnnihilator","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Eightfold.ConnectedSumAnnihilator","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.ConnectedSumProbe.annihilator_not_monotone","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.ConnectedSumProbe.annihilator_not_monotone","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/ConnectedSumAnnihilator.lean#L106-L122","doc":"**The recurrence ideal is not monotone under pointwise multiplication.**\n\nThere are towers `f`, `g` and a first-order operator `P` with `P ∈ A_f` and\n`P ∉ A_{f·g}`. Concretely `f ≡ 1`, `g = 2^n`, `P = L − 1`: the residual is `2^n`,\nnonzero at every colour.\n\nSince `J_{K₁ # K₂} = J_{K₁} · J_{K₂}` pointwise, this is exactly the statement\nthat **a map `A_{K₁} × A_{K₂} → A_{K₁ # K₂}` cannot be \"carry the annihilator\nacross\"**. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.ConnectedSumProbe.not_annihilates_pow_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.ConnectedSumProbe.not_annihilates_pow_two","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/ConnectedSumAnnihilator.lean#L98-L104","doc":"**`L − 1` does NOT annihilate `1 · 2^n`.** The residual at colour `n` is\n`2^n`, which is nonzero everywhere — so the failure is not an edge case at one\ncolour. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.ConnectedSumProbe.annihilates_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.ConnectedSumProbe.annihilates_one","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/ConnectedSumAnnihilator.lean#L94-L96","doc":"The constant tower `f ≡ 1` is annihilated by `L − 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.ConnectedSumProbe.mulPow_not_mul_both","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.ConnectedSumProbe.mulPow_not_mul_both","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/ConnectedSumAnnihilator.lean#L84-L90","doc":"**`M` is NOT fully multiplicative**, witnessed over `ℚ`: applying it to both\nfactors squares the weight. Stated as a concrete inequality so it is falsifiable\nrather than a slogan. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.ConnectedSumProbe.mulPow_mul_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.ConnectedSumProbe.mulPow_mul_left","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/ConnectedSumAnnihilator.lean#L78-L82","doc":"**`M` passes to one factor.** Diagonal multiplication is \"half\"\nmultiplicative — the asymmetry with `shift_mul` is the whole obstruction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.ConnectedSumProbe.shift_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.ConnectedSumProbe.shift_mul","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/ConnectedSumAnnihilator.lean#L73-L76","doc":"**`L` is fully multiplicative on pointwise products.** It shifts both\nfactors; it does not act on one tensor leg. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.ConnectedSumProbe.annihilates","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.ConnectedSumProbe.annihilates","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/ConnectedSumAnnihilator.lean#L66-L69","doc":"`P` annihilates `f`, for the first-order operator `a₀ + a₁·L`. This is the\norder-1 case of `QuantumTorusAJ.act2`; order 1 suffices for the obstruction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.ConnectedSumProbe.mulPow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.ConnectedSumProbe.mulPow","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/ConnectedSumAnnihilator.lean#L63-L64","doc":"Diagonal multiplication by `q^n` — the `M` generator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.ConnectedSumProbe.shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.ConnectedSumProbe.shift","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/ConnectedSumAnnihilator.lean#L58-L61","doc":"The colour shift `L`, in the function model of `QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorusAJ`\n(there `sigma a = fun N => a (N + 1)`). Colours are indexed by `ℕ` here so the\nfile stays over a plain `CommRing` (AGENTS.md §7c). ","signatureChunk":0}]}